,"rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T14:36:48-07:00","id":1401192,"title":"","content":"Any non-american city to see what happens in the rest of the world. <br /> Fall of London can not be seen as a City by night book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T15:24:34-07:00","id":1401203,"title":"","content":"<b>LA By Night</b> by Jason Carl with all of the characters from his game.<br /> <br /> Or <b>Washington D.C. by Night</b>.<br /> <br /> Actually, I think a better idea would be to do a book of say, 5 cities with just the major players of both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T15:32:45-07:00","id":1401204,"title":"","content":"<b>Cities that already had a book:</b><br /> <br /> -<b>Washington DC</b>: A nominally anarch city ruled by a Lasombra Methuselah besides being the capital of the USA. I think there's a lot of interesting stuff going on here and a lot of potential to evolve the setting as a whole.<br /> <br /> -<b>Los Angeles</b>: I want the show status quo to be aknowledged. It's a more traditional anarch domain but now it is contested by the invading Camarilla and that's really something that changes the usual dynamic of these things as the Camarilla normally is the sect that gets &quot;sieged&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cities that never had a book:</b><br /> <br /> -<b>Milan</b>: Giangaleazzo's coup was the prototype for the Lasombra's mass defection from the Sabbat and now he's one of the fewLasombra princes holding domain over an important city (the other styilg himself as an &quot;anarch emperor&quot;...). That and the new status quo with the Hecata make the city very interesting to me.<br /> <br /> -<b>Moscow</b>: There's just a lot of ground to uncover there, from the fall of Baba Yaga to the potential of conflict with the lupines. Most of it was never explored in depth before so it's exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T17:40:06-07:00","id":1401233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401203#post1401203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>LA By Night</b> by Jason Carl with all of the characters from his game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard pass. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or <b>Washington D.C. by Night</b>. </div> </div> </div>Do this. This city has enough old lore and new changes to build something dynamic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, I think a better idea would be to do a book of say, 5 cities with just the major players of both. </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting direction for it; basically the city as a setting and something like the leadership (Prince and Primogen for a Cam city).<br /> <br /> I'd like to see something South American so we can see Drowned Legacies. I'd like to see something Eastern European to hit 'old places of the world' for Gehenna Crusade content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T17:45:55-07:00","id":1401237,"title":"","content":"With a few notable exceptions, the By Night books were atrocious disappointments. I only found Chicago By Night and Montreal By Night to be useful. Whatever flaws they had, what they did right was so good it more than made up for it. I had a few friends who were extremely fond of one or two of the other By Night books, but those were never consistent (one liked DC a lot, another LA, and a third New Orleans) and they were not supported by others. The rest were utter dreck that no one was found of. My general review of them was that someone picked a city, spent a few hours in the library looking up important landmarks and city history events, xeroxed a tourist map, and then dropped their own PCs and the PCs of their friends in some homebrew campaign and called it a day.<br /> <br /> In my opinion no matter what city is chosen, the following must be done in order to write a successful book:<ul><li>The history of the city needs to be expressed in the vampire NPCs of the city. Around half of the NPCs should be natives to the city at different time periods, so we can see how the city changed in the lives of the NPCs.</li> <li>The NPCs need to be interesting in the sense of how they are useful in showing the setting to the PCs. I thought far too many city NPCs in published books were obviously of the category &quot;this is the writer's favorite PC&quot;. They were quirky and powerful, but nothing about them screamed &quot;this city&quot; or were of a nature I thought they were a good tool for the ST in running the game.</li> <li>The city's history needs to be relevant to the current setting of the game. At any point in time of that city, we should be able to visualize the vampires of that era and think they &quot;fit&quot;. We don't need to be told that vampires did certain actions that caused real historical events (though used judiciously and with taste, this isn't bad). But we should be able to see how events or trends were used as covers for vampire relevant events like praxis seizures, anarch uprisings, Sabbat crusades, successful vampire hunts, changes in primogen leadership, etc.</li> <li>The NPCs should be varied and interesting enough that an ST has good hooks for any potential plot they want to run. That means covering a lot of the general hooks of vampire that players are often interested in - someone who can help someone on the path to Golconda, someone who can connect the PCs to a rival sect, characters that embody one of the classic conflicts of the game (Anarchs vs Prince, Camarilla (in sense of Justicars, Archons) vs Prince, Prince vs Primogen, Loyalist Sabbat against Conservative Sabbat, character upset that X happened in history vs character happy that X happened in history).</li> <li>The idea of secret Methusalehs influencing a city was old hat after the first Chicago By Night book. Avoid it entirely. However, I do think it is an important for the book to have some kind of central mystery that explains many strange and unusual events in the city as a &quot;chronicle tentpole&quot;. Just make it new and interesting.</li> <li>The setting acknowledges that there are more supernatural present than just vampires - and therefore clears out certain places or organizations as belonging in the domain of something else whether it be mages, lupines, wraiths, hunters, etc.</li> <li>The book should serve as &quot;tool box&quot; in the sense it teaches the readers how to run a particular style of game or event. CbN showed us a weak prince that appeared strong (Lodin was weak via the Primogen, but appeared strong to neonates). DCbN showed us a strong price that dominated his Primogen. Show us something else. LAbN failed in showing an interesting anarch city. So maybe we get a city that is actually interesting. Or show us a city chronicle that is meant to go through the stages of a Sabbat Crusade. Talk us through the various steps and how the Bishops are planning each phase, so the ST can know how the PCs can aid or thwart it. Or show us a city where Archons operate, and how that interferes with the other vampires in the city. Or a city with a &quot;reforming&quot; Prince who is trying to change things. Or how a Conclave actually works and can be run by an ST. Or a city with an incredible threat to it (Lupines, Inquisition, Independent Ghouls on a rampage). There are lots of things that can be done. What a &quot;tool box&quot; does well is teach the readers by example of how to create your own city of that kind.</li> <li>Don't waste space on a prolonged single &quot;story&quot; in the book. Many potentially good sourcebooks were ruined when a lame plot took up half of the book. Several pages of interesting city plots based on NPCs and unique conflicts of the book are fine. Even needed. But I don't need half the book taken up with a verbose plot railroad.</li> <li>Coterie charts are essential.</li> <li>Ghouls are often neglected in the game. Make sure they have their own section, and what &quot;ghoul life&quot; is like in case playes want to play a ghoul, or ST wants to run a ghoul campaign. Or even just cool things that might be done with the NPC ghouls of a character's background.</li> <li>Don't make metaplot important. But it is OK, even encouraged, that important elements of vampire history be reflected in the NPCs of the city.</li> </ul>I think it would work best to select a city not already having a By Night book. Best to strike new ground.<br /> <br /> I will not be buying it of course. I consider V5, like the Revised era Metaplot, to essentially be fan fiction. Maybe good and interesting fan fiction at times, but it only represents a particular person's chronicle. And while I might find it fun to play in, it does not represent an official canon to me. So unless there is something particularly spectacular (cool NPCs, a great chronicle tentpole, effective tool box, etc.) I won't be buying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-14-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T23:59:32-07:00","id":1401287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401107#post1401107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copenhagen. Because Denmark. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That could be potentially really cool with Christiania as an Anarch zone, it has a lot of promise. Like is it a Cam city with an autonomous Anarch center in Christiania or the whole city in control by the Anarchs by now?<br /> <br /> Budapest might be another neat spot to cover, it being at an edge where both the Cam and older Tzimisce have an interest, but probably better to wait until they do the reveal on whatever the Sabbat have been up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T01:36:17-07:00","id":1401294,"title":"","content":"Copehagen would also be interesting in that it's half an hour, a sea straight and an international border away from another city. I do think that Black Fox has a point and that Copenhagen might not have quite the right sort of history for the current setting, in terms of how human trends and events would be reflected in the city's Kindred.<br /> <br /> I don't see any European city getting a By Night book, as interesting as it could be unless it was a new Anarch domain with entrenched elders displaced.<br /> <br /> Tijuana/San Diego could be interesting or El Paso/Ciudad Juarez.<br /> <br /> I'd like there to be a Kyiv or Trieste by night.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26282-lacheur","name":"Lacheur","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T05:37:45-07:00","id":1401326,"title":"","content":"Damascus by Night: War, Gehenna crusade, Ashirra, Camarilla comandos, Sabbat guerrillas, ancient creatures awakening...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T18:24:03-07:00","id":1401414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401237#post1401237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Ghouls are often neglected in the game. Make sure they have their own section, and what &quot;ghoul life&quot; is like in case playes want to play a ghoul, or ST wants to run a ghoul campaign. Or even just cool things that might be done with the NPC ghouls of a character's background.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add that this should probably apply to certain non-ghoul mortals as well. Potential allies/contacts, as well as potential enemies, including vampire hunters. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T19:01:09-07:00","id":1401416,"title":"","content":"New Orleans needs an updated sourcebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T10:58:42-07:00","id":1401514,"title":"","content":"We've seen lots of By Night books that explore vast cities with demi-god rulers. I'd like to see a compilation book that explores cities which are smaller or more isolated than most domains.<br /> <br /> How do social and political dynamics change at smaller scales? How do vampires avoid lupines and hunters? How do they monitor media for masquerade breaches with limited resources? How does a city remain stable when the ruling vampires are lower-powered, possibly even book standard, vampires? What happens to clan and sect identity in such an incestuous city? What happens when it is not just a small city, but a small nation? Ordinarily, a local Prince might have influence over the mayor, but in Lichtenstein or Latvia the Prince might reasonably have influence at the UN or NATO.<br /> <br /> So, some cities I'd like to propose:<ul><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azores\" target=\"_blank\">Azores by Night</a>: An archipelago of islands, and a state of Portugal situated in the middle of the Atlantic. Despite a population of 250k, it serves as a vital stopover point for both air and sea traffic. A key location for kindred traveling between Europe and the Americas while avoiding daytime flights. Do local kindred fight to maintain strict neutrality or have the islands been seized by one of the sects?</li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nur-Sultan\" target=\"_blank\">Nur-Sultan by Night:</a> A planned city which was made the capital of Kazkhstan in the late 90's, when it had only 300k people. It has experienced a population boom, growing to 1.2 million people. This growth led to vast building projects and a futuristic... if somewhat sterile... <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/@51.1280785,71.4323502,3a,75y,242h,85.85t/data=!3m8!1e1!3m6!1sAF1QipOL-36Vexkl140W66gmgE-z7U1aZeybev1vUHnf!2e10!3e11!6shttps:%2F%2Flh5.googleusercontent.com%2Fp%2FAF1QipOL-36Vexkl140W66gmgE-z7U1aZeybev1vUHnf%3Dw203-h100-k-no-pi-0-ya74.59769-ro-0-fo100!7i5376!8i2688\" target=\"_blank\">city-scape</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murmansk\" target=\"_blank\">Murmansk by Night:</a> This Russian city (the largest city north of the Arctic Circle) has a population of a half million. It's a port city expected to be on the rise as climate change opens year-round seaways. How do kindred survive the <a href=\"https://www.timeanddate.com/sun/russia/murmansk\" target=\"_blank\">midnight sun of summer and noontime gloom of winter</a> at such latitudes?</li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Sahara\" target=\"_blank\">Western Sahara by Night:</a> This land of conflict hangs on where the desert meets the sea. It has a land area larger than the UK, but a population equivalent to just Cornwall. The Moroccans, Mauritanians, and Spanish all have made claims to this nearly empty land.</li> <li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belize\" target=\"_blank\">Belize by Night: </a>This former British colony in Central America is incredibly diverse despite having a population of only 400k. Despite its small size and less than vibrant economy, a kindred who influences its political leaders would have a hand in international affairs, including UN and Commonwealth membership.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T18:52:56-07:00","id":1401589,"title":"","content":"Preferably an Islamic city, cause I'd like more information on Modern Nights Ashirra. (There was only a little in Cairo by Night.) Maybe Istanbul, connects nicely to Constantinople by Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T16:23:48-07:00","id":1401986,"title":"","content":"There is a <i>Miami By Night</i> book on the Storyteller's Vault. I believe that for the smaller cities, fans with some writing skill who know the area well (locals or lived there for a while) could fill in a lot of interesting areas by adding in historical research.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/317465.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain\" target=\"_blank\"> Miami by Night: The Miami Food Chain - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Miami by Night: The Miami Food Chain - For most Cainites, the Sabbat is synonymous with the grit and violence of Detroit, the backstabbing politics of Mexico C </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T18:09:24-07:00","id":1401997,"title":"","content":"antarctic research station! Reenact the THing with vampires/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T02:24:42-07:00","id":1402028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401997#post1401997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">antarctic research station! Reenact the THing with vampires/</div> </div> </div> </div>This, kind of, has been done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Cities/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/title.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Cities/\" target=\"_blank\"> VtM - Cities and Chronicles </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Cities/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Cities/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A Killing Frost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T05:39:59-07:00","id":1402050,"title":"","content":"I would love to see:<br /> - An updated New Orleans<br /> - Tangiers, Morroco<br /> - Detroit<br /> - LA by Night based on the show<br /> - Seattle based on the shows/Bloodlines 2<br /> - Paris<br /> - Munich, Germany as a complete book (as opposed to the teaser in Cults of the Blood Gods)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T06:36:03-07:00","id":1402059,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Alaska by Night?<br /> <br /> Jamaica by Night would also be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T22:18:38-07:00","id":1402190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1402059#post1402059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... Alaska by Night?<br /> <br /> Jamaica by Night would also be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Sugar and Slaves</i> by Richard Dunn would be a good book for historical context for the Jamaica By Night. The book is on Barbados and Jamaica and will connect to U.S. and Latin America history and the Atlantic Slave Trade. It also talks about how sugar was made in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T02:26:50-07:00","id":1402205,"title":"","content":"I read Shadow of the Wind just after I\u2019d visited Barcelona (not intentionally - as in, I didn\u2019t accidentally read a book, but I didn\u2019t seek out a book set there) and it totally took me back there. It was my first thought as soon as I saw this thread! I didn\u2019t really like the book, but the setting kinda saved it from being a total loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For those who are fans of the <a href=\"https://kisslightnovels.info\" target=\"_blank\">read light novels</a> L. Death note another note is an excellent light novel","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26308-realfox","name":"RealFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T12:29:28-07:00","id":1402276,"title":"","content":"I'd like a <i>good </i>treatment of New Orleans as a Hecata-controlled city. Then I think we could leave the US behind for the most part and focus on other parts of the world, with writers who know what the hell they're talking about. It would probably be best to bundle the cities in with other relevant expansions, such as a revision of the modern Ashirra that comes with a redo of the Cairo setting, or Tokyo that comes with a look at the shape of the Camarilla in East Asia. But the trick there is that these would need to be made by people in the know, and the bar is a lot higher than it used to be, while the market for them might be smaller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T14:06:06-07:00","id":1402289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1402276#post1402276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like a <i>good </i>treatment of New Orleans as a Hecata-controlled city. Then I think we could leave the US behind for the most part and<u><b> focus on other parts of the world, with writers who know what the hell they're talking about</b></u>. It would probably be best to bundle the cities in with other relevant expansions, such as a revision of the modern Ashirra that comes with a redo of the Cairo setting, or Tokyo that comes with a look at the shape of the Camarilla in East Asia. But the trick there is that these would need to be made by people in the know, and the bar is a lot higher than it used to be, while the market for them might be smaller.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded part cannot be stressed enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T17:04:24-07:00","id":1402334,"title":"","content":"You\u2019d want pick a city that is large in population, sadly rife with violent crime and has a history. <br /> <br /> New Orleans in the US is a good option, so is a number of US cities, but we have Chicago well developed already. I wish they would add to the Fall of London with a city campaign, and I could see Paris or Berlin or Moscow or Instanbul. What about Rio de Janeiro, Johannesburg, Lagos or Mumbai? Maybe Melbourne, Sydney or Auckland if you want to get some Australasian cities in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T20:52:14-07:00","id":1402355,"title":"","content":"Berlin would be a fine Anarch signature city, if they didn't want to do L.A. again, though L.A. is hot shit because of the computer game and the streaming show.<br /> <br /> Mostly I think one signature city per sect is enough, which is part of the reason I think a Hecata New Orleans would be worthwhile, plus an Ashirra city like Cairo, and an Anarch city.<br /> <br /> New York can be the &quot;whatever the hell they are this week&quot; city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T20:56:03-07:00","id":1402357,"title":"","content":"All things considered, I'd prefer something akin to Damnation City, providing all the tools and advice to design your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T01:17:45-07:00","id":1402380,"title":"","content":"You guys ever play <i>pandemic </i> where like, the famous cities of some major countries get a spot, chinese cities take three spots, but the USA alone has seven, California having two of those seven *?<br /> (*Because San-Diego clearly deserves to be up there with Giants like Jakarta, Istambul, Beijing...) <br /> Somehow it does better than the world of Darkness. <br /> <br /> <br /> Shanghai <br /> Bangkok <br /> Barcelona<br /> Kyiv<br /> Bucharest<br /> <br /> Though I feel some of these names aren't exciting to American audiences (what's a Bucharest and why is it by night?) You could probably start with an edgy name to draw people in (CITY OF BLOOD: BUCHAREST BY NIGHT) and exciting cover artwork. <br /> <br /> But literally, the publisher should just go through a list of populous cities, pick any that look like Gotham, Pick any with a high corruption rate or turbulent history. <br /> <br /> I don't read by-nights. I didn't get around to finishing OG chicago. I just make up my own stories for cities. I might be more interested if this stuff looked good, but it doesn't. <br /> <br /> American cities are also like, the least By-Night place I'd be interested in reading into. First thing; There's only modern history, so I don't have to do much of my own research. Second thing, being in the anglosphere has exposed me to enough 'murica and knowing how America is a fun, farcical Oligarchy where.... Anyhow, It gives me lots of my own ideas on how to do things. Kyiv though, the opposite; Rich history I would need to spend good time reading up on, I'm not well exposed to how things work there so a city book would be giving me something new and interesting... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T04:15:33-07:00","id":1402391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1402357#post1402357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All things considered, I'd prefer something akin to Damnation City, providing all the tools and advice to design your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damnation City is extremely useful even for a VTM game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3740-baron-john","name":"Baron John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3740_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T00:32:28-07:00","id":1402532,"title":"","content":"Barcelona? In what part of Mexico is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T03:53:17-07:00","id":1402560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1402532#post1402532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barcelona? In what part of Mexico is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this is sarcasm because it is the capital of Catalonia and famous for it sepparatis crisis in Spain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T05:05:28-07:00","id":1402571,"title":"","content":"No, it is because some old declarations of George Bush era about Spain being in Mexico and speaking &quot;mexican&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T13:13:26-07:00","id":1402664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1402571#post1402571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it is because some old declarations of George Bush era about Spain being in Mexico and speaking &quot;mexican&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>WTF?!? I can hardly believe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T13:57:42-07:00","id":1402676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1402664#post1402664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WTF?!? I can hardly believe it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find any citation of it even after multiple web searches. <br /> <br /> <br /> Fun Fact: Most of the Spanish translations of books you see in book stores are in Castilian Spanish, the &quot;official&quot; Spanish national language from northern and central Spain. The irony is that bookstores stock these in an effort to attract Latin American immigrant customers, but they tend to avoid these books because Castilian Spanish is a different dialect than that used in Mexico, Central or South America. And Caribbean Spanish is also an entirely different dialect. (My cousin lived in Columbia for ten years and pointed this out to me one time.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T23:37:58-07:00","id":1402750,"title":"","content":"A few examples:<br /> <br /> -Jeb Bush about the Spanish &quot;Republic&quot;: <a href=\"https://elpais.com/diario/2003/02/18/espana/1045522807_850215.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://elpais.com/diario/2003/02/18...07_850215.html</a><br /> <br /> -Donald Trump using images of Melilla as part of Mexico: <a href=\"https://www.europapress.es/internacional/noticia-trump-utiliza-imagenes-salto-valla-melilla-ilustrar-frontera-mexico-20160104221401.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.europapress.es/internaci...104221401.html</a><br /> <br /> I am still looking for the old declarations of the Geoge Bush comittee, I think he was not himself, but another member of the government.<br /> <br /> About the dialects, I am from eastern Spain, I speak castillian and catallonian languages, but even if I understand perfectly the south-american accent, sometimes it is too much musical for us. It is not a matter of words, but pronunciation, I think. Spanish is in Spain a hard and low language, nearly monotone. But there are important efforts to unify their users, there have published years ago some Pan-Hispanic dictionaries and institutions as the Instituto Cervantes are trying to maintain some degree of consensus between the different countries. Is like Australian, North-American, Irish and British English languages, any place has is traits, but it is easy to recognize the meanings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 07-14-2020, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T15:45:36-07:00","id":1414661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401237#post1401237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>The book should serve as &quot;tool box&quot; in the sense it teaches the readers how to run a particular style of game or event. CbN showed us a weak prince that appeared strong (Lodin was weak via the Primogen, but appeared strong to neonates). DCbN showed us a strong price that dominated his Primogen. Show us something else. LAbN failed in showing an interesting anarch city. So maybe we get a city that is actually interesting. Or show us a city chronicle that is meant to go through the stages of a Sabbat Crusade. Talk us through the various steps and how the Bishops are planning each phase, so the ST can know how the PCs can aid or thwart it.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I remember a discussion about repurposing the Blood Bond adventure, with the duo of infiltrators (Rigaud &amp; Wade) spurring &quot;alternate versions&quot; of the plot, involving Lawrence Ballard x Horatio Ballard, agent Gregory Stephens &amp; Jacob Schumpeter's daughter x Juggler &amp; Schumpeter, to create a general climate of paranoia &amp; distrust around the use and abuse of the Bond, to them slip rumors about Maldavis' origin (it was pre-2nd ed Chicago), along with some about a ritual to shatter the bond, for maximum paranoia....<br /> <br /> And sidetrack everybody of their <b>real </b>target - the local kindred ghouls, turned into a troops of exceptionally experienced &amp; well-informed shovelheads, full of anger, resentment &amp; bonds shattered. Is that fine for a start?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401237#post1401237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Coterie charts are essential.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>A book can never have too many coterie/clique relationship charts, never.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401237#post1401237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Ghouls are often neglected in the game. Make sure they have their own section, and what &quot;ghoul life&quot; is like in case playes want to play a ghoul, or ST wants to run a ghoul campaign. Or even just cool things that might be done with the NPC ghouls of a character's background.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Once as a joke made a &quot;ghouls waiting table&quot; in the Succubus Club or some Elysium i forget. Honestly, that thing snowballed so much crazy my players started to watch out for it <b>more </b>than the Prince's court....The &quot;shovelhead army&quot; from above was one twisted shake-up of that nucleus of the cast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1401237#post1401237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would work best to select a city not already having a By Night book. Best to strike new ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, new places to spur the imagination of players and STs in new ways is always welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-19-2020, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T16:10:05-07:00","id":1414665,"title":"","content":"Hmm ... Omaha by Night. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T19:36:17-07:00","id":1414679,"title":"","content":"For my two cents on the topic I think that the concept of the &quot;by night books&quot; is flawed at its root due to the setting.<br /> <br /> In a fantasy setting you can release a book that talks about a place because there is no other source of information about it. With the WoD setting Google is your City Book because it allows you to go to any point in that locations history, rather than the small slice of time that the By Night book is relevant. Also most of the By Night books tend to be designed to be game line or concept exclusive. A good example is the San Francisco by Night book. If you don't want KotE in your game that book is practically useless.<br /> <br /> A better design model would be to do By Night books as splat neutral books that more or less is just a big list of historical places and events that could tie into each splat line as story hooks or ST inspiration. Avoid the premade characters and power structure route, most of the groups I have played in tended to scrap the premade characters and power structures and thus it is just wasted page space.<br /> <br /> Also if you can't get a writer from the actual area, don't bother trying to make the book. It becomes blatantly obvious how little the writers understand how the given city interacts with the local power structures from surrounding cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T22:09:17-07:00","id":1414692,"title":"","content":"I've not really been super into the city by night books and maybe this is just because I'm rewatching the TV series right now, but Fargo by night sounds awesome. It could be a general Northern mid-west book and cover a lot of ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T23:59:36-07:00","id":1414698,"title":"","content":"More Asian cities<br /> <br /> I will be glad to see Beijing/Shanghai/etc. by Night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 09-20-2020, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T00:35:26-07:00","id":1414882,"title":"","content":"While I would like to read about more about the Ashirra I think one city finally deserve a new by Night book.<br /> <br /> Berlin. This city has so much wasted potential with its history and contradictions. And as far as I know there is no by night book.*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *We don't speak of this abomination and waste of paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T04:17:13-07:00","id":1414897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1414882#post1414882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I would like to read about more about the Ashirra I think one city finally deserve a new by Night book.<br /> <br /> Berlin. This city has so much wasted potential with its history and contradictions. And as far as I know there is no by night book.*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *We don't speak of this abomination and waste of paper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Berlin by Night</i> is only the fourth-worst city book for <i>Vampire</i>. And it really isn't much good, which says something about how astronomically terrible some of the other books are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T07:40:25-07:00","id":1414913,"title":"","content":"Maybe rather than a single book in a single city, the approach could be;<ul><li>An anthology, like the Dark Era for CoD.</li> <li>A series of articles or blog (on different cities) posts behind a paywal.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T13:18:01-07:00","id":1414957,"title":"","content":"I go with one American and one foreign City, so I think LA would be most appropriate for Vampire, and for a foreign city Paris, waiting till they are ready to do Rio or Mexico City justice by waiting for them to make the splats like the drowned legacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T15:04:14-07:00","id":1414973,"title":"","content":"While I do occasionally joke about stuff like Le Claire, Iowa by Night, I do seriously believe that a sourcebook about setting Vampire in smaller towns and even semi-rural areas would be pretty useful. A game where the PCs make up anywhere from a fifth to half of the local vampire population is going to be a lot different than one with the sort of population of Chicago or Berlin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T15:14:52-07:00","id":1414974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1414882#post1414882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*We don't speak of this abomination and waste of paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>The really sad thing about Berlin by Night is that Berlin in 1992/1993 was a really great place to set a Vampire game, what with both sides of the city's strong punk and other music subcultures from the 70s and 80s and the East German life under the watch of the Stasi to influence neonates and play into a lot of the game's overall themes, plus stuff from the Weimar era and 19th century as influences for ancilla. Instead it felt like this odd alternate universe in which WW2 was about the only thing of importance that had happened in the city's history. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T16:24:59-07:00","id":1414987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1414957#post1414957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go with one American and one foreign City, so I think LA would be most appropriate for Vampire, and for a foreign city Paris, waiting till they are ready to do Rio or Mexico City justice by waiting for them to make the splats like the drowned legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, PLEASE no more Drowned Legacies. They are awful, specially to people from South America.<br /> <br /> The Tlacique were a really interesting concept as long as they were an offshoot of either the aztec methuselahs, the Baali or pre-Montano Lasombra, but when that concept was thrown to the trash, the drowned legacies became the most uninteresting, absolute zero hype of Vampire The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 09-21-2020, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T17:13:30-07:00","id":1414992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1414973#post1414973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do occasionally joke about stuff like Le Claire, Iowa by Night, I do seriously believe that a sourcebook about setting Vampire in smaller towns and even semi-rural areas would be pretty useful. A game where the PCs make up anywhere from a fifth to half of the local vampire population is going to be a lot different than one with the sort of population of Chicago or Berlin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree - this would be a solid concept. So many of the larger cities are surrounded by smaller cities, it could create an interesting dynamic if the prince in the large city tried to control the smaller ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T18:05:27-07:00","id":1414997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1414992#post1414992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree - this would be a solid concept. So many of the larger cities are surrounded by smaller cities, it could create an interesting dynamic if the prince in the large city tried to control the smaller ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that small towns might be where the Anarchs would have a better chance of success, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T18:46:14-07:00","id":1415000,"title":"","content":"Just in America there are more than 200 cities with a mortal population between 100K and 500K. Which would be large enough for a small number of vampires to fight over power, be terrible people, and deal with invasions from the outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T01:40:55-07:00","id":1415278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1414973#post1414973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do occasionally joke about stuff like Le Claire, Iowa by Night, I do seriously believe that a sourcebook about setting Vampire in smaller towns and even semi-rural areas would be pretty useful. A game where the PCs make up anywhere from a fifth to half of the local vampire population is going to be a lot different than one with the sort of population of Chicago or Berlin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Colony could have been such a rulebook as it attempted to depict vampires of multiple domains, often relatively small, in a region. But the sourcebook had several flaws that prevented it. First, it had a strange hook about British vampires trying to regain control of the &quot;colonies.&quot; While I understand why they used that hook, it just didn't work. Second, too much of the book was taken up by a lame &quot;plot&quot;. It would have been better to devote those pages to more NPCs, more coteries, and how individual domains interacted with each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-24T05:27:07-07:00","id":1415291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401105-what-city-should-get-a-book-next?p=1415278#post1415278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dark Colony could have been such a rulebook as it attempted to depict vampires of multiple domains, often relatively small, in a region. But the sourcebook had several flaws that prevented it. First, it had a strange hook about British vampires trying to regain control of the &quot;colonies.&quot; While I understand why they used that hook, it just didn't work. Second, too much of the book was taken up by a lame &quot;plot&quot;. It would have been better to devote those pages to more NPCs, more coteries, and how individual domains interacted with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>in a more perfect world, I like to believe Dark Colony would have been part of a trilogy of regional sourcebooks alongside Southern Gothic and Western Nights that looked at what made those regions culturally distict as well as how to run Vampire in the vein of New England Gothic, Southern Gothic, and Western/Western Gothic respectively. Perhaps with a fourth about the Caribbean (Blood-Dimmed Tides, with WoD: Dark Waters being the name of the ocean book).<br /> <br /> Because, yes, spending an entire book about New England focusing on vampires trying to refight the American Revolution was such a waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 09-24-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}